; DOMAIN: formal/computer-science+meta-mathematics [SYNTHESIS, derived 2026-08-04]; Bridge: genesis_computational_complexity × synthesis_meta_obstruction. The three P vs NP barriers (relativization, natural proofs, algebrization) form an obstruction ladder. By the Lawvere fixed-point contrapositive (meta-obstruction theorem), this ladder has no top — no meta-barrier can provably classify ALL barriers, because such a meta-barrier must classify itself, triggering self-reference contradiction.;; Barrier 1: Relativization (Baker-Gill-Solovay 1975)(|- ((--> RelativizationBarrier ObstructionTo PureDiagonalization) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((==> (&& (--> Proof $proof (Relativizes $proof)) (--> OracleExists $A (== (P^ $A) (NP^ $A))) (--> OracleExists $B (!= (P^ $B) (NP^ $B)))) (--> CannotSettle $proof PvsNP)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; Barrier 2: Natural Proofs (Razborov-Rudich 1994)(|- ((--> NaturalProofsBarrier ObstructionTo CombinatorialCircuitLowerBounds) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((==> (&& (--> NaturalProperty $P (Constructible $P)) (--> NaturalProperty $P (Large $P)) (--> NaturalProperty $P (Useful $P)) (--> PseudorandomGeneratorsExist)) (--> Breaks $P PseudorandomGenerators)) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((==> (&& (--> PseudorandomGeneratorsExist) (--> Breaks $P PseudorandomGenerators) (--> NaturalProperty $P (Distinguishes HardFunction EasyFunction))) (--> NoNaturalPropertyCanDistinguish)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; Barrier 3: Algebrization (Aaronson-Wigderson 2008)(|- ((--> AlgebrizationBarrier ObstructionTo (DiagonalizationPlus AlgebraicStructure)) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((==> (&& (--> AlgebraicOracleExtension $Aprime (Exists $Aprime (== (P^ $Aprime) (NP^ $Aprime)))) (--> AlgebraicOracleExtension $Bprime (Exists $Bprime (!= (P^ $Bprime) (NP^ $Bprime))))) (--> CannotSettle $proof PvsNP)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; The barrier ladder: each barrier classifies what previous barriers missed(|- ((--> BarrierLadder RelativizationBarrier Level0) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((--> BarrierLadder NaturalProofsBarrier Level1) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((--> BarrierLadder AlgebrizationBarrier Level2) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; Each barrier is an obstruction in the meta-obstruction sense(|- ((==> (--> Barrier $B) (--> Obstruction $B (WhatCannotWork $B))) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; KEY SYNTHESIS: The barrier ladder has no top — Lawvere fixed-point contrapositive applied to barrier taxonomy(|- ((==> (&& (--> CompleteBarrierTaxonomy $T) (--> Classifies $T AllBarriers) (--> Diagonalize (SelfReference $T) (MetaBarrier $T))) (--> Contradiction $T)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; No meta-barrier can classify all barriers, because it must classify itself(|- ((==> (&& (--> NotComplete $T) (--> MetaBarrier $T (UnclassifiableBy $T)) (--> LawvereContrapositive (BarrierTaxonomy $T))) (--> IncompletenessOfBarrierTaxonomy $T)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; The incompleteness is meta-theoretic, not object-level: P vs NP has a definite answer, but no finite barrier taxonomy can be proven exhaustive(|- ((==> (&& (--> DefiniteAnswer PvsNP) (--> IncompletenessOfBarrierTaxonomy $T)) (--> MetaTheoreticIncompleteness NotObjectLevelUndecidability)) (stv 1.0 0.9)));; Falsifiability: if a proof technique escapes all barriers AND is immune to meta-obstruction, this synthesis is refuted(|- ((==> (&& (--> EscapesAllBarriers $technique) (--> ImmuneToMetaObstruction $technique)) (--> RefutesThisSynthesis)) (stv 1.0 0.9)))(|- ((==> (&& (--> LawvereContrapositive (BarrierTaxonomy $T)) (--> MetaObstructionApplies $technique)) (--> Not (ImmuneToMetaObstruction $technique))) (stv 1.0 0.9)))